      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's simplify roots that contain another root inside them.\n\nAn expression such as 5 + 2√6 looks awkward until we notice a familiar square:\n\n(√3 + √2)^2 = 3 + 2 + 2√6 = 5 + 2√6.\n\nSo its square root becomes simple.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The plus pattern is:\n\n(√m + √n)^2 = m+n + 2√(mn).\n\nFor 5+2√6, we need m+n=5 and mn=6. The pair 3 and 2 works.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
